Package: comdynamite
Title: Linking Traits, Phylogenies and Biogeography in Metacommunities
Version: 0.6.1
Authors@R: person("Diogo B.", "Provete", email = "dbprovete@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Methods that link traits, phylogenies, biogeography and
    metacommunities, to analyse data and to simulate it. Analyses include the
    node regression of Leibold et al. (2010) <doi:10.1111/j.1461-0248.2010.01523.x>,
    with biogeographic events and restricted null models, the phylogenetic
    gradient analysis of Peres-Neto et al. (2012) <doi:10.1890/11-0494.1>, and the
    phylogenetic community composition and beta diversity tests of Peres-Neto
    and Kembel (2015) <doi:10.1007/s11258-014-0405-0>. Simulations follow the
    process-based model of Thompson et al. (2020) <doi:10.1111/ele.13568>, with
    environmental filtering, competition, demographic stochasticity and
    dispersal in spatially implicit or grid landscapes. Species traits can carry
    phylogenetic signal or evolve under an Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process, and
    competition can be structured by relatedness. Rule-based assembly follows
    Kraft et al. (2007) <doi:10.1086/519400>. Models were implemented from the
    published equations.
